      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's incredibly sharp. The idea of her \"moral high ground\" being a \"shield of privilege\" is exactly the kind of intellectual gut-punch the scene needs. It moves the character from a simple antagonist to something much more complex and, frankly, more damning.\n\nCan you actually write out the dialogue for this specific moment? I want to see the Senator's lines—give him those heavy, surgical arguments that strip away her illusions. And for her, I want her to respond with those soaring, idealistic calls for justice, but I want her dialogue to feel like it's struggling to find footing against his points. I want the audience to feel the weight of his \"grim necessity\" crushing her \"abstract purity.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
